<title>UK: Salomon appoints new fixed income head for Germany.</title>
<headline>Salomon appoints new fixed income head for Germany.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Brothers said in a statement on Thursday it had appointed Jurgen Guba as head of fixed income capital markets for Germany.</p>
<p>He will be based in Frankfurt and report to the head of Salomon Brothers' German operations, Dan Lee.</p>
<p>Guba joins the firm from Commerzbank in Frankfurt where he was area executive responsible for Germany, Britain, Ireland and the Netherlands.</p>
<p>He worked for the Bundesbank from 1980 to 1986 in the economic and research department.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
